  "rationale": "Both answers express the same ordinary sense. Indonesian akhir bulan is also an accepted Malay expression, while Malaysian references explicitly define hujung bulan as akhir bulan. The national split is therefore materially overstated as a categorical different-common-word relation, although hujung bulan remains a useful Malaysian preference. No false-friend contrast is supported.",
